Title: Host SDL3: core audio/timer on SDL3 under BOXER_HOST_SDL3, SDL2 kept
Repository: boxer (https://github.com/alinebee/Boxer.git)
Date: 2026-10-02
Author: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Base-Commit: 0062fc18e154cde6cef3bf3329be4b0658597e31
Preceding-Patches:
  0001-aros-host-sdl-seam.patch
  0002-aros-config.patch
  0003-mount-colon-paths.patch
Problem: The host layer is moving to SDL3 (SDL2 is deprecated upstream; linking the SDK's SDL2 brings gl.library/Mesa in before main on both ABIs). SDL3 removed SDL_OpenAudio/SDL_LockAudio/SDL_PauseAudio, the SDL_mutexP/V macros, and returns Uint64 from SDL_GetTicks; Boxer's port layer paused audio by calling SDL_PauseAudio directly. SDL2 must stay buildable as the comparison point.
Solution: boxer_host_sdl.h includes <SDL3/SDL.h> when BOXER_HOST_SDL3 is defined (SDL_ENABLE_OLD_NAMES for SDL_mutex, SDL_SwapLE32, AUDIO_S16SYS; SDL_mutexP/V and a 32-bit SDL_GetTicks macro), SDL2 otherwise. mixer.cpp: MIXER_LockHost/UnlockHost (SDL2 global audio lock, or the SDL3 stream lock that SDL holds during the stream callback); SDL3 opens SDL_OpenAudioDeviceStream on the default playback device with S16/2/rate, requests blocksize frames by hint and takes the device's buffer size as blocksize; a stream callback clears a chunk, runs the unchanged MIXER_CallBack and puts the data; MIXER_Stop destroys the stream (joins the device thread). New MIXER_SetHostPaused (replaces the port's direct SDL_PauseAudio) and MIXER_GetHostStats (callbacks, frames, underruns, overflows, emulated vs host ms) for both hosts. Without BOXER_HOST_SDL3 the device code is SDL2's as before; the counters are added on both.
Platform-Scope: AROS x86_64 ABIv11 and mainline v1 (non-Apple builds); __APPLE__ builds unaffected (seam not used there; mixer counters and MIXER_SetHostPaused compile on any host).
Upstream-Status: local-only
Verification: 2026-10-02: build-core/build-ui/build-smoke with BOXER_HOST=sdl3 and sdl2 on ABIv11 (GCC 10.5.0) and mainline v1; SDL3 builds carry no GLBase/SDL2Base libset. Runtime: tested on ABIv11 only; mainline build/link only.
Removal-Condition: When SDL2 is no longer needed as a comparison build, drop the SDL2 branches; when the core is replaced, drop the patch.

